<activity xml:id="act-FirstParametricCurve" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Our First Parametric Curve</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            We'll begin by exploring the parametrically defined curve:
            <md>
                <mrow>x \amp = t^2-3t-4</mrow>
                <mrow>y \amp = 1-t^2</mrow>
            </md>
            for <m>0 \leq t \leq 4</m>.
        </p>
        <p>
            For each task, we'll use the following visualization:
        </p>
        <interactive platform="doenetml" width="95%" aspect="1:2">
            <slate surface="doenetml">
                <xi:include parse="text" href="../doenet/FirstParametricCurve.doenet"/>
            </slate>
        </interactive>
    </introduction>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                In Step 1, how does the graph of <m>x=t^2-3t-4</m> give us information about the horizontal movement of our parametric curve?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Fill in the table with the <m>x</m>-values at different values of <m>t</m>. Describe the horizontal motion of the parametric curve using this information.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                In Step 2, how does the graph of <m>y=1-t^2</m> give us information about the vertical movement of our parametric curve?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Fill in the table with the <m>y</m>-values at different values of <m>t</m>. Describe the vertical motion of the parametric curve using this information.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                In Step 3, confirm that the point follows the path you constructed. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</activity>